// DataTwist Error Demonstrations
// Each expression below produces a runtime or parse error

// ============================================================
// 1. Undefined identifier
// ============================================================
// Accessing a name that was never bound
nonexistent-variable

// ============================================================
// 2. Did-you-mean suggestion
// ============================================================
// A typo close enough to trigger a suggestion
user is {name: "Alice"}
users.name    // Undefined: 'users'. Did you mean 'user'?

// ============================================================
// 3. Type error: string + number
// ============================================================
// Arithmetic between incompatible types
"hello" + 5   // Cannot add string and integer

// ============================================================
// 4. Map over non-collection
// ============================================================
// Applying map to a scalar value
42 |> map _ * 2   // Cannot map over Long: expected a list or object

// ============================================================
// 5. Object destructuring of non-object
// ============================================================
// Trying to destructure a number as an object
{name} is 42   // Object destructuring expects an object, got Long

// ============================================================
// 6. Division by zero (integer)
// ============================================================
5 / 0   // Divide by zero

// ============================================================
// 7. Calling a non-function
// ============================================================
x is 42
x 5   // Not a function

// ============================================================
// 8. Parse error (invalid syntax)
// ============================================================
// Missing arrow in function literal
[x  x * 2]   // Parse error: expected '->'
